**Reproduced:** `ParserError: Unexpected token Unless` — `src/lexer.rs:25` emits the token, `src/parser.rs` had zero `TokenKind::Unless` arms.

**Implemented** `Statement::Unless { condition, body }` across `src/parser.rs` (new `parse_unless()`, added to `opens_block()` so `MAX_BLOCK_DEPTH` bounds it), `src/vm.rs`, `src/analyzer.rs`, `src/linter.rs`, `src/formatter.rs`, `src/bytecode/codegen.rs`. Matches `docs/GRAMMAR.md:220` exactly: required `then`, no `else`. Codegen uses `Not` + `JumpIfFalse` because no `JumpIfTrue` exists.

**Tests:** 15 `#[test]` in new `tests/unless_test.rs` + 3 Redblue blocks. Each class proven able to fail by mutation — inverting the VM condition gives 6 failures; deleting the codegen `Not` gives `the bytecode VM printed ["body"] for unless yes, expected []`.

**One thing I fixed in passing and flagged:** `tests/redblue_suite_test.rs:28` kept a hand-written block-keyword list that omitted `unless`, so the harness silently truncated any test body containing it and wrongly reported "has no assertion". I couldn't add a Redblue-level test for this feature without fixing it. Residual class recorded in FINDINGS.md.

**Gates:** `cargo fmt --check` pass · `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` pass, zero warnings · `cargo test --all-targets` **590 passed, 0 failed** · `cargo test --doc` 1 passed · all `examples/*.rb` and `modules/*.rb` exit 0.

**Gate 4 was not run: `rbops/` does not exist in this checkout** (`ls rbops/` → no such directory; `git ls-files | grep rbops/` → empty), and my instructions forbid looking for the pipeline elsewhere. REPORT.md records it as NOT RUN rather than claiming a pass.
